+/******************************************************************************
+ * next/ v12b: the ALIGNED backward (and, without a run table, the CQS-off one).
+ *
+ * On a 128-aligned CQS task every tile the backward visits is fully live or
+ * fully masked (results/ultimate/align_census.json: mixed 0.000%), so the
+ * CQS-on backward needs neither the per-element mask path nor any per-tile
+ * verdict. The census (cqs_census_bwd.cu) lists each column block's live m
+ * blocks as runs in descending m -- the order v11's backward visits them in --
+ * and this kernel is upstream FlashAttention-2's seqk-parallel backward loop
+ * driven by that list. b3: the function below IS the text of
+ * compute_dq_dk_dv_1colblock as v11x compiles it (-DCQSA_BWD_NO_CQS: upstream's
+ * loop with our contract), with the `#ifdef CQSA_BWD_NO_CQS` sides selected and
+ * every v12b change marked `next/ v12b` and folded away by `if constexpr` /
+ * constant `m_step == 1` when Use_runs = false, so the CQS-off instantiation is
+ * v11x's loop. (b1/b2 were hand-specialised copies whose ptxas schedule ran 3-5%
+ * slower than v11x's; see docs/ultimate/progress/P2_backward_kernel.md.)
+ * With runs: the first visited m block is the first run's hi; the next one is
+ * decided where the Q prefetch first needs it (m - 1 inside a run, the next
+ * run's hi at a boundary); the Q / dO / LSE / dPsum / dQaccum pointers take
+ * upstream's one-block step plus the gap (pointer arithmetic, no predication);
+ * the sQ double buffer toggles per VISITED tile instead of by m parity. Fully
+ * masked tiles, including the fully masked diagonal tile of a non-owner column
+ * block, are absent; the owner diagonal takes upstream's causal mask and the
+ * ragged tail upstream's !Is_even_MN path. A call whose census finds a mixed tile
+ * (or more runs than slots) runs on LEGACY (v11's CQS backward) instead, decided
+ * on the device. Dpsum_smem: dP_sum staged in smem by cp.async next to the Q
+ * prefetch instead of read from global memory (default for CQS-on calls; env
+ * CQSA_V12B_DPSUM_SMEM=0/1 overrides it per call for A/B runs).
+ *
+ * Contract kept from v11 (the engine's): global lse in, caller-supplied
+ * dsoftmax_sum (or the preprocess pass), fp32 dq_accum by atomics, dk/dv
+ * written in Element. Production configuration only: no dropout, local
+ * window, alibi, softcap, varlen or numden mode, d == kHeadDim
+ * (cqs_bwd_aligned_eligible); anything else runs on LEGACY.
+ *
+ * Exactness vs v11's CQS backward: a live tile runs the same instructions on
+ * the same data in the same (descending m) order, so acc_dk / acc_dv are
+ * bit-identical; a dead tile contributes exact zeros in v11 (its GEMMs are
+ * guarded off, or, for a ragged dead tile v11 cannot prove dead, P == 0
+ * everywhere), so leaving it out changes nothing. dQ is accumulated by fp32
+ * atomics across column CTAs in any case (non-deterministic order).
+ ******************************************************************************/
